  "transcript_source": "captions",
  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 4.36,
      "e": 6.74,
      "text": "(suspenseful music)"
    },
    {
      "s": 6.74,
      "e": 9.95,
      "text": "- [Reporter] In the year 2000, the entire world was shocked"
    },
    {
      "s": 10.07,
      "e": 12.16,
      "text": "by the sinking of the submarine, Kursk,"
    },
    {
      "s": 12.47,
      "e": 16.64,
      "text": "tragically killing all 118 Russian submariners on board."
    },
    {
      "s": 17.07,
      "e": 19.6,
      "text": "This maritime disaster marked a turning point"
    },
    {
      "s": 19.6,
      "e": 21.66,
      "text": "in submarine rescue cooperation."
    },
    {
      "s": 24.46,
      "e": 25.88,
      "text": "Just three years later,"
    },
    {
      "s": 25.9,
      "e": 28.77,
      "text": "NATO established an international hub of submariners"
    },
    {
      "s": 28.9,
      "e": 30.41,
      "text": "that could go anywhere in the world"
    },
    {
      "s": 30.41,
      "e": 31.66,
      "text": "to save those in trouble,"
    },
    {
      "s": 31.85,
      "e": 36.77,
      "text": "no matter the place, no matter the conditions."
    },
    {
      "s": 41.25,
      "e": 42.98,
      "text": "- We don't have any distinction between"
    },
    {
      "s": 42.98,
      "e": 44.69,
      "text": "save a life for another life."
    },
    {
      "s": 44.84,
      "e": 46.49,
      "text": "For us, it's important brotherhood."
    },
    {
      "s": 46.49,
      "e": 48.14,
      "text": "For us, it's important to be here"
    },
    {
      "s": 48.22,
      "e": 50.0,
      "text": "and be ready to save a life"
    },
    {
      "s": 50.4,
      "e": 52.81,
      "text": "whatever countries belongs this life."
    },
    {
      "s": 53.84,
      "e": 55.49,
      "text": "- [Reporter] Being submariner is one of the"
    },
    {
      "s": 55.49,
      "e": 57.34,
      "text": "most high-risk jobs in the world."
    },
    {
      "s": 57.64,
      "e": 60.68,
      "text": "It's no wonder then that all submariners are a family,"
    },
    {
      "s": 61.02,
      "e": 63.21,
      "text": "and the only common enemy is the sea."
    },
    {
      "s": 63.79,
      "e": 66.43,
      "text": "NATO's International Submarine Escape and Rescue"
    },
    {
      "s": 66.45,
      "e": 69.46,
      "text": "Liaison Office or ISMERLO is at the heart"
    },
    {
      "s": 69.46,
      "e": 71.18,
      "text": "of this international cooperation"
    },
    {
      "s": 71.41,
      "e": 74.39,
      "text": "and is open to any nation that uses submarines."
    },
    {
      "s": 78.45,
      "e": 81.34,
      "text": "- The ISMERLO organization include 41 nations,"
    },
    {
      "s": 81.34,
      "e": 83.22,
      "text": "and everybody are cooperating"
    },
    {
      "s": 83.31,
      "e": 88.12,
      "text": "to improve this kind of skill, save a life."
    },
    {
      "s": 88.29,
      "e": 90.21,
      "text": "- [Reporter] These kind of skillS are hard-won"
    },
    {
      "s": 90.21,
      "e": 92.02,
      "text": "and meticulously preserved."
    },
    {
      "s": 92.31,
      "e": 93.69,
      "text": "NATO trains regularly"
    },
    {
      "s": 93.8,
      "e": 96.11,
      "text": "on submarine search and rescue exercises."
    },
    {
      "s": 100.81,
      "e": 102.41,
      "text": "- It's really important we train it"
    },
    {
      "s": 102.41,
      "e": 104.35,
      "text": "because save a life and"
    },
    {
      "s": 104.51,
      "e": 106.65,
      "text": "on the bottom of the sea is not so easy."
    },
    {
      "s": 107.38,
      "e": 109.52,
      "text": "- [Reporter] The exercises also help share knowledge"
    },
    {
      "s": 109.52,
      "e": 112.14,
      "text": "and strengthen the bonds between partners worldwide."
    },
    {
      "s": 113.67,
      "e": 116.15,
      "text": "- The most important value of this exercise is that"
    },
    {
      "s": 116.15,
      "e": 119.05,
      "text": "we have a lot of observers come from all over the world."
    },
    {
      "s": 119.32,
      "e": 122.77,
      "text": "More than 30 nations are observing us and working with us"
    },
    {
      "s": 122.89,
      "e": 124.12,
      "text": "in very close way."
    },
    {
      "s": 127.47,
      "e": 128.97,
      "text": "- [Reporter] It's also a chance to test out"
    },
    {
      "s": 128.97,
      "e": 131.24,
      "text": "the latest technology in under water rescue"
    },
    {
      "s": 131.24,
      "e": 132.31,
      "text": "from each country."
    },
    {
      "s": 133.28,
      "e": 136.01,
      "text": "Ranging from specifically designed rescue chambers,"
    },
    {
      "s": 136.1,
      "e": 138.21,
      "text": "to mini-submarine rescue vehicles."
    },
    {
      "s": 145.15,
      "e": 147.44,
      "text": "- Each system has it's own benefits."
    },
    {
      "s": 147.44,
      "e": 149.05,
      "text": "It depends on the conditions."
    },
    {
      "s": 149.47,
      "e": 150.69,
      "text": "With submarine rescue chambers,"
    },
    {
      "s": 150.69,
      "e": 153.04,
      "text": "they are very good at working at shallow water."
    },
    {
      "s": 153.64,
      "e": 156.28,
      "text": "In deeper water in more difficult conditions,"
    },
    {
      "s": 156.52,
      "e": 159.1,
      "text": "then rescue chambers are of limited use"
    },
    {
      "s": 159.1,
      "e": 161.35,
      "text": "and you need to have a proper rescue vehicle."
    },
    {
      "s": 161.89,
      "e": 163.74,
      "text": "- [Reporter] In a real rescue situation,"
    },
    {
      "s": 163.74,
      "e": 166.45,
      "text": "commanders would have a range of solutions to choose from"
    },
    {
      "s": 166.45,
      "e": 168.77,
      "text": "to make sure personnel get out alive."
    },
    {
      "s": 169.57,
      "e": 171.09,
      "text": "And of course, there's a website"
    },
    {
      "s": 171.09,
      "e": 173.41,
      "text": "where all nations can share information."
    },
    {
      "s": 174.32,
      "e": 176.51,
      "text": "Being a submariner remains one of the most"
    },
    {
      "s": 176.51,
      "e": 178.13,
      "text": "difficult jobs in the world."
    },
    {
      "s": 178.46,
      "e": 180.38,
      "text": "But today, the international community"
    },
    {
      "s": 180.38,
      "e": 183.12,
      "text": "is cooperating to improve submarine rescue."
    },
    {
      "s": 183.36,
      "e": 185.67,
      "text": "And NATO is at the forefront."
    }
  ],
